==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʃiːr/|lang=ang}}, {{SAMPA|/Si:r/|lang=ang}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{proto|Germanic|skīro||skīzo|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old High German {{term|scira|scīra|lang=goh}}.

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|head=scīr|g=f}}

# [[office]] (status of an official)
# [[district]] (under an official or governor)
# administrative region, [[shire]] (consisting of a number of [[hundred]]s or [[wapentake]]s, ruled jointly by an alderman and a sheriff)

=====Declension=====
{{ang-decl-noun|scīr|scīra, scīre|scīre|scīra, scīre|scīre|scīra|scīre|scīrum}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[scirgerefa|scīrġerēfa]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gem|ang}} ''*skeira-''.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|skire|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|skir|skīr|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|schier||white, grey|lang=nl}}, German {{term|schier||pure|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|skirr|skírr|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|skir|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐍃𐌺𐌴𐌹𐍂𐍃|sc=Goth|lang=got}}  Related to {{term|scinan|lang=ang}}.

